<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Antigua</h1><p class="st-meta">1632 CE – 1981 CE · capital St John's</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">English and later British sugar colony that hosted the Royal Navy's main Leeward Islands base and became independent as Antigua and Barbuda in 1981.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>English colonists from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-saint-christopher">Saint Kitts</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-warner">Edward Warner</a> settled Antigua in 1632. The French briefly occupied it in 1666, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-breda-1667">Treaty of Breda</a> in 1667 restored English rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-codrington-1640-1698">Christopher Codrington</a> began large-scale <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> planting in 1674, and the island was soon covered with plantations and windmills.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Antigua had its own governor, council and assembly, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-johns-antigua-and-barbuda">St John's</a> served as capital of the wider <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/leeward-islands-colony">Leeward Islands colony</a> for long periods. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar</a> estates relied on enslaved Africans, and a planned rising in 1736 was crushed with savage executions. English Harbour, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelsons-dockyard">Nelson's Dockyard</a>, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy's</a> chief base in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leewards</a>. Antigua freed its enslaved people in 1834 without the apprenticeship system used elsewhere.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After emancipation the island remained poor and dependent on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>. Labour activism led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vere-bird">Vere Bird</a> built a political movement in the mid-20th century. Antigua became an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies-associated-states">Associated State</a> in 1967 and gained independence, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redonda">Redonda</a>, as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/antigua-and-barbuda">Antigua and Barbuda</a> on 1 November 1981.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1632 CE – 1981 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.18%;width:6.95%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1632 CE – 1981 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>St John's</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Edward Warner, Christopher Codrington</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/antigua-and-barbuda">Antigua and Barbuda</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Antigua, Antigua</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=colony-of-antigua" aria-label="Colony of Antigua on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3001 1533 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Antigua lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M3320 1799h0M3305 2036h0M3318 1798h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3321 1789h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M3321 1789h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Antigua and Barbuda. <a href="/atlas?year=1806&amp;focus=colony-of-antigua">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
